%T A063501 83217782,571314626,4010758480,28722086297,209359671771
%N A063501 Number of prime-sextuplets up to 10^n.
%C A063501 A sextuplet (p, p+4, p+6, p+10, p+12, p+16) is counted when its largest member p+16 is at most 10^n; thus a(1) = 0 although p = 7 < 10.
%H A063501 Norman Luhn, <a href="https://www.pzktupel.de/counting/PI_06.php">PI_6(10^n)</a>
%H A063501 <a href="/index/Pri#primepop">Index entries for sequences related to numbers of primes in various ranges</a>
%e A063501 a(12)=50408 because there are 50408 prime-sextuplets up to 10^12.
%Y A063501 Cf. A022008 (initial members of prime-sextuplets).
